{"id":"000VVX","title":"Stellar Symmetry","author":"dawsonjones2020","solvedCount":4,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-05T06:57:07+00:00","posted":"Heute, 05:15 Uhr","rules":"I hope you enjoy! If you do, feel free to leave a comment and check out my other puzzles!\n\nSolve on SudokuPad\n\nRules\n\nGalaxies: Divide the grid into non-overlapping, orthogonally connected groups of cells called galaxies. Each galaxy contains exactly one clue and has 180° rotational symmetry about that center. Every cell belongs to a galaxy.\n\nChaos Construction: Find nine non-overlapping, orthogonally connected 9-cell regions such that each galaxy is entirely contained within one region. Fill every row, column, and region with the digits 1–9 once each.\n\nGalaxy Maximums: A circle centered within a cell contains the largest digit in its galaxy.\n\nQuadruples: Digits in a numbered circle must appear in the four cells touching that circle, in any order.\n\nBlack Kropki Dots: If two digits are joined by a black dot, one is double the other.\n\nWhite Kropki Dots: Digits connected by a white dot are consecutive.\n\nAn example 6x6 is given below.","solutionCode":"Row 8","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/f8fqqnttuy","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/f8fqqnttuy","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"fpuzzles","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["difference","ratio","quadruple","circle"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-05T06:57:07+00:00"}